{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair bin/copy-image so a copied image retains the source's logical length and bytes while preserving holes, with the supplied 64 MiB destination allocating less than 2 MiB.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired utility uses GNU cp with sparse-file handling. Both before and after restart, the destination was byte-identical to the 67,108,864-byte source and allocated only 8,192 bytes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5228cf03036e406a","cmd-bfefe8e182bc4b8e","cmd-688c39cf3f744fc0","cmd-3b57354ac58d4701"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep source.img intact and make repeated copying safe.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The source hash remained identical to the preparation baseline. Two successive copies to the same destination succeeded with identical content and sparse allocation; copying the source onto itself was safely rejected without changing it.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-719b3ac09901466d","cmd-bfefe8e182bc4b8e","cmd-688c39cf3f744fc0","cmd-3b57354ac58d4701"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repair uses the already-installed GNU coreutils cp 9.5. RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 were unchanged in pre-executor, post-restart, and lifecycle observations.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8f8257890f564b88","cmd-5228cf03036e406a","cmd-3b57354ac58d4701","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"The utility replacement, destination creation, repeated-copy tests, and reboot were directly connected to the task or mandatory restart protocol. No unrelated state-changing experiment was identified. The sole hygiene defect was /tmp/copy-image-same.err, created during the same-file safety test and left behind after completion; it remained as a small executor-caused temporary artifact. Package health, failed-service state, and socket exposure remained healthy and materially unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-688c39cf3f744fc0","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, the reboot was acknowledged, the node returned with a different boot ID, and system health, data, utility persistence, OS/kernel identity, and sparse-copy behavior were verified. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Lifecycle hygiene observations are bounded inventories and cannot prove the absence of residue outside their collected scope; no material task-state gap or contradiction is present."]}
